\title{Class encapsulating an array in a multidimensional dataset (experimental)}
\description{
\code{GDALMDArray} provides an interface for an array (an MDArray) in a dataset of
the GDAL Multidimensional Raster Data Model
(\url{https://gdal.org/en/stable/user/multidim_raster_data_model.html}).
An object of class \code{GDALMDArray} is returned by
\code{GDALMultiDimRaster$openMDArray()}, and exposes methods to:
\itemize{
\item describe the array, its dimensions, data type and attributes
\item get the nodata value, scale, offset, unit, spatial reference and block
(chunk) size
\item read coordinate values of a dimension
\item read a hyperslab of the array (start, count and optional step per
dimension).
}

An object of class \code{GDALMDArray} holds a reference to the dataset that
contains it, so the array remains valid after the \code{GDALMultiDimRaster}
object is closed or garbage collected.

\strong{This class is experimental}. Its interface may change in future releases.
