the \code{$} operator. \strong{Note that all arguments to class methods are required
and must be given in the order documented.}

Dimension indexes and offsets are 0-based, as in other \strong{gdalraster} class
methods. Dimensions are always given in the array's own order, slowest
varying first (e.g., \verb{time, lat, lon}).
